          "quote": "**(b) Rindler wedge congruence.** In an inertial chart $(x^0,x,y,z)$ consider $\\Phi(\\theta,\\rho,y,z):=(\\rho\\sinh\\theta,\\rho\\cosh\\theta,y,z)$ on $\\mathbb R\\times(0,\\infty)\\times\\mathbb R^2$, with $\\theta\\in\\mathbb R$ and $\\rho>0$. Then $\\Phi$ is a smooth bijection onto the right wedge $W:=\\{(x^0,x):x>|x^0|\\}$, with smooth inverse $\\rho=\\sqrt{x^2-(x^0)^2}$, $\\theta=\\tfrac12\\log\\bigl((x+x^0)/(x-x^0)\\bigr)$ ([[thm-hyperbolic-identities-and-derivatives]], [[def-hyperbolic-functions]]); the pullback of $\\eta$ is $g=-\\rho^2d\\theta^2+d\\rho^2+dy^2+dz^2$; the field $n:=\\rho^{-1}\\partial/\\partial\\theta$ is a future unit timelike field on $W$ whose congruence is Born rigid and irrotational, with acceleration $a=\\nabla_nn=\\rho^{-1}\\partial/\\partial\\rho$, hence $\\eta(a,a)=\\rho^{-2}$; its rest slices $\\theta=const$ are hyperplanes orthogonal to $n$ with induced metric $d\\rho^2+dy^2+dz^2$ independent of $\\theta$",
