          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $c > 0$ and let $x : I \\to A$ be a $C^{1}$ future timelike worldline ([[def-sr-regular-causal-curve-and-worldline]]) with proper-time function $\\tau(s) = c^{-1}\\int_{s_0}^{s}\\sqrt{-\\eta(x'(u),x'(u))}\\,du$ for a base point $s_0 \\in I$ ([[def-sr-proper-time]]). Then: **(i)** $\\tau$ is differentiable at every $s \\in I$, with one-sided derivatives at the endpoints of $I$, and $$\\tau'(s) = c^{-1}\\sqrt{-\\eta\\bigl(x'(s),x'(s)\\bigr)} > 0$$ for every $s \\in I$; since $\\tau'$ is this composition of continuous maps, $\\tau$ is $C^{1}$ on $I$. **(ii)** $\\tau$ is strictly increasing on $I$, hence injective, and its image $J := \\tau[I]$ is an order-convex subset of $\\mathbb{R}$ with at least two elements, so $\\tau : I \\to J$ is a bijection. **(iii)** The inverse $\\rho : J \\to I$ of $\\tau$ is continuous and strictly increasing, and it is differentiable at every point $\\tau(s)$ of $J$ with $$\\rho'\\bigl(\\tau(s)\\bigr) = \\frac{1}{\\tau'(s)} = \\frac{c}{\\sqrt{-\\eta(x'(s),x'(s))}} > 0 ;$$ hence $\\rho$ is $C^{1}$ on $J$. **(iv)** The reparametrized curve $y := x \\circ \\rho : J \\to A$ is a $C^{1}$ future timelike worldline whose tangent at the proper-time parameter $\\tau(s)$ is $$(x \\circ \\rho)'\\bigl(\\tau(s)\\bigr) = \\frac{x'(s)}{\\tau'(s)} = \\frac{c\\,x'(s)}{\\sqrt{-\\eta(x'(s),x'(s))}} ;$$ in particular $y$ is parametrized by its own proper time up to the additive constant of the base point.",
