          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix $n\\ge1$ and a commutative ring $R$. A function $F:M_n(R)\\to R$ is **column-multilinear** when, with all other columns fixed, it is additive and compatible with scalar multiplication in each selected column.\n\nIt is **alternating** when $F(A)=0$ whenever two columns of $A$ are equal. It is **antisymmetric** when interchanging two columns negates its value. It is **normalized** when $F(I_n)=1$. These conditions are stated over the ring itself and do not assume that $2$ is invertible.",
