     "fact": "F1",
     "source": "def-em-electric-moments",
     "source_section": "Definition",
     "quote": "For the Lebesgue branches (a) and (b) assume Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$), inherited from the exact measure interface ([[def-countable-choice]]); the finite sums in branch (c) are defined and computed without Choice. Let the laboratory region, its chart, its spatial Euclidean structure and its units be those of [[def-em-lab-geometry]] and [[def-em-si-conventions]], and let $\\delta_{ij}$ be the Kronecker symbol in the $\\delta$-orthonormal basis $(e_1,e_2,e_3)$ of the frame, with $|y|$ the Euclidean norm of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]. This definition assigns **source moments** to a static charge distribution in the fixed-time reading of [[def-em-electrostatic-regime]] (d) and (e). Three branches are declared. (a) [Absolutely continuous branch] Let $a>0$ and let $\\rho\\in L^1(\\mathbb R^3)$ be real ([[def-l-one-of-a-measure]]) and vanish $\\lambda_3$-almost everywhere outside the closed ball $\\overline B_a(0)=\\{y:|y|\\le a\\}$ ([[def-metric-ball]], [[def-measure-null-set-and-almost-everywhere]]). The **total charge** $Q$, the **dipole moment** $p$, the **degree-$l$ Cartesian moments** $M_{i_1\\dots i_l}$ and the **traceless quadrupole** $Q_{ij}$ are $$Q:=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\rho\\,d\\lambda_3,\\qquad p_i:=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}y_i\\,\\rho(y)\\,d\\lambda_3(y),\\qquad M_{i_1\\dots i_l}:=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}y_{i_1}\\cdots y_{i_l}\\,\\rho(y)\\,d\\lambda_3(y)\\ (l\\ge1),$$ $$M^{(0)}:=Q,\\qquad M_i:=p_i,\\qquad Q_{ij}:=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\bigl(3y_iy_j-|y|^2\\delta_{ij}\\bigr)\\rho(y)\\,d\\lambda_3(y),$$ with $l\\ge1$ and indices in $\\{1,2,3\\}$; units are C for $Q$, C m for $p$, C m$^l$ for the degree-$l$ Cartesian moment and C m$^2$ for $Q_{ij}$, and all integrals are in the sense of [[def-integral-over-a-measurable-set]] and [[def-integrable-real-and-complex-functions-and-their-integrals]]",
