     "quote": "Assume Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$), with the exact meaning of [[def-countable-choice]]. Let $P_l$ denote the real vector space of homogeneous polynomials of degree $l$ on $\\mathbb R^3$, $H_l=\\ker(\\Delta:P_l\\to P_{l-2})$ with $P_k=\\{0\\}$ for $k<0$, and let spherical harmonics of degree $l$ be the restrictions of $H_l$ to $S^2$, with unnormalised surface measure $d\\Omega$ of total mass $4\\pi$. Then $P_l=H_l\\oplus|x|^2P_{l-2}$, $\\dim H_l=2l+1$, harmonics of distinct degree are orthogonal in $L^2(S^2,d\\Omega)$, and the union over $l$ of the spaces of spherical harmonics admits a complete orthonormal basis of $L^2(S^2,d\\Omega)$ ([[def-orthonormal-family-complete-orthonormal-system-and-hilbert-basis]]). For any real orthonormal basis $Y_{lm}$, $m=1,\\dots,2l+1$, of degree-$l$ harmonics the addition theorem holds: $$\\sum_{m=1}^{2l+1}Y_{lm}(n)Y_{lm}(n')=\\frac{2l+1}{4\\pi}P_l(n\\cdot n'),$$ where $P_l$ is the Legendre polynomial of the convergent zonal kernel lemma ([[lem-em-convergent-legendre-kernel]])",
