     "source": "lem-em-convergent-legendre-kernel",
     "source_section": "Statement",
     "quote": "For $z\\in[-1,1]$ define the real polynomial $P_l(z)=\\pi^{-1}\\int_0^\\pi\\bigl[z+i\\sqrt{1-z^2}\\,\\cos\\theta\\bigr]^l\\,d\\theta$, $l\\in\\mathbb N_0$. Then $P_l$ is a real polynomial of degree at most $l$ with $|P_l(z)|\\le1$ on $[-1,1]$, $P_l(1)=1$, and for $|q|<1$ the series $\\sum_{l\\ge0}q^lP_l(z)$ converges absolutely and uniformly on $[-1,1]$ with $$(1-2qz+q^2)^{-1/2}=\\sum_{l=0}^{\\infty}q^lP_l(z),$$ where the branch is the analytic square root equal to $1$ at $q=0$ ([[def-series-of-real-functions]], [[thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series]])",
