     "quote": "Adopt as a physical postulate of this framework the following four equations for the fields of [[def-em-fields]] and the sources of [[def-em-sources]] on the laboratory region $U\\cong I\\times\\Omega$ of [[def-em-lab-geometry]], with $\\mu_0>0$, $c>0$, $\\varepsilon_0=(\\mu_0c^2)^{-1}$ and the SI units of [[def-em-si-conventions]]. (a) [Smooth branch] Let $E,B$ be jointly $C^1$ fields with the additional derivatives required by each equation existing and continuous, and let $\\rho,J$ be continuous. Then, with the divergence and curl of [[def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field]] and the partial derivative $\\partial_t$ at fixed position of [[def-directional-and-partial-derivatives]], $$\\operatorname{div}E=\\rho/\\varepsilon_0,\\qquad \\operatorname{div}B=0,\\qquad \\operatorname{curl}E=-\\partial_tB,\\qquad \\operatorname{curl}B=\\mu_0J+c^{-2}\\partial_tE.$$ (b) [Weak branch] Let instead $E,B$ be locally integrable $\\mathbb R^3$-valued fields and $\\rho,J$ locally integrable scalar and vector fields on $I\\times\\Omega$, identified with their regular distributions ([[def-regular-distribution-from-a-locally-integrable-function]], [[thm-locally-integrable-functions-embed-in-distributions]])",
