          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be order-convex with at least two elements, let $x_0\\in I$, and let $p,q:I\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuous. The IVP $y'+py=q$, $y(x_0)=y_0$, has exactly one solution on $I$, namely\n\n$$y(x)=\\exp(-P(x))\\left(y_0+\\int_{x_0}^x\\exp(P(t))q(t)\\,dt\\right),\\qquad P(x)=\\int_{x_0}^x p(t)\\,dt.$$",
